# Shop details

Canonical business facts. These are **not** in the database — the `location`
table holds only `name`, `code`, and `status`, so there is no address column to
read from. Use these values instead of inventing placeholders.

## Toronto (location code `TOR`)

- **Legal entity:** OTOMOTO TORONTO MOTO INC.
- **Address:** 99 River Street, Toronto, ON M5A 3P4, Canada
- **Phone (call + text):** 647-424-1088
- **Site:** https://www.torontomoto.com — app at https://service.torontomoto.com

Hours: Mon–Fri 12:00–19:00, Sat 10:00–16:00, Sun closed. Closed on Victoria Day,
Canada Day, Civic Holiday, Labour Day, and Thanksgiving.

## Ottawa (location code `OTT`)

A second active location exists in the `location` table. Its address is unknown —
ask rather than reusing the Toronto address for it.

## Where this matters

- **Twilio:** use the legal entity name and Toronto address for regulatory
  address records, toll-free verification, and Trust Hub business profiles.
  Canadian carriers reject mismatches against the registered business name.
- **647-424-1088 is the number customers already text.** The public site tells
  them to text before dropping a bike off, so prefer porting it into Twilio over
  buying a new number, otherwise the shop silently loses that thread.
- Contracts, invoices, and customer-facing documents should use the legal entity
  name, not the "Toronto Moto" trade name.
